    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 95846,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95846.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, yes, and I think that was really good because, you know, it's noted now that what is happening with inflation and really what people are experiencing such a supermarket and at the gas station, but, you know, it's going to take a little time. But I think that if Congress, we work together and work with the presidents on these issues, we can, you know, just think about so many women that have to work for us because they can't afford daycare, you know, and so as a result, if we work through some of the legislation that we have, you know, we passed the American Rescue Act, which really helped a great deal. And then we passed the bipartisan infrastructure bill, which also helped a great deal. We've created a lot of jobs. We just got to make sure that people take these jobs, but inflation is going to be with us for a while. But we got to bring down prescription drug calls. You know, we got to put people back to work. You know, we got to give people confidence in that it's going to work out. And we want to make sure that when people are sitting by the table, at the kitchen table, trying to figure out how they're going to pay their bills, is that we've tied to give them some relief. We need tax credit for the average person, just like we've done for billionaires for years and years. We pay no taxes. It is incredible that some of the richest people in the world pay zero taxes in our middle class are the one that care in this country. So we got to focus. And I think one of the things we focus more on in middle class And for people who are going day to day that they could have confidence in what's happening in America.",
